\n(b)  whether the Government has implemented any schemes to provide financial \nassistance to various projects of classical language and if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  the details of the funds provided for each classical language during each of the \nlast three years, language-wise;  \n(d)  whether the Government has received any proposal regarding the classical \nlanguage projects during the last three years; and  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the response of the Government thereon? \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR CULTURE & TOURISM \n(PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n \n(a) There are six Indian languages namely; Tamil, Sanskrit,  Telugu Kannada \nMalayalam, Odia which have been accorded Classical Language status. \n(b)&(c)  For Sanskrit language, Rashtriya Sanskrit Sansthan (RSKS), New Delhi under \nHuman Resource Development (HRD) Ministry, has been established as the \nnodal authority for promoting the language. \n\nFor Classical Telugu and Classical Kannada, HRD Ministry has established \nCentres of Excellence for Studies in respective languages in Central Institute of \nIndian Languages (CllL), Mysore during 2011.  \nIn respect of Classical Tamil Language,  an autonomous organization namely, \nCentral Institute of Classical Tamil (CICT), Chennai has been established at \nChennai by HRD Ministry. \nln addition, University Grants Commission has approved a Centre for Classical \nLanguages in Telugu in University of Hyd erabad and a Centre for Classical \nLanguages in Kannada in Central University of Karnataka. \nDetails of grants released/allocated by the Ministry of Human Resource \nDevelopment to RSKS, CICT and CIIL which are working for the promotion of \nclassical Languages, is as under :- \n(In lakh) \nNo. Institute Language 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 \n1. Rashtirya Sanskrit Sansthan Sanskrit 19831.06 21437.99 23115 \n2. Central Institute of Classical Tamil Tamil 1059 465 770 \n3. Central Institute of Indian \nLanguages \nTelugu 100 99 107 \nKannada 100 99 107 \n \n(d)&(e)  HRD Ministry is considering setting up of establishment of Centres of \nExcellence for Classical Odia and Classical Malayalam. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |172", "t": "Data Regarding Schools and Colleges", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n172\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n3\nRD\n \nMARCH, 2020\n \n \nPRODUCTION OF RED GRAM\n \n \n*172. \n    \nSHRI KOMATI REDDY VENKAT REDDY: \n \n             \nSHRI BANDI SANJAY KUMAR: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \n \nAND FARMERS\n \nWELFARE  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Union Government is aware of the massive production of red gram (pigeon \npea) in the country especially in the State of Telangana this year; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe measures being considered to procure the same through NAFE\nD or any other \nGovernment agency; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether any request has been received from the State Government of Telangana for \nprocurement of excess red gram from the State; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nif so, the details thereof and the action taken in this regard?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\ne\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\ne\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION \nNO.\n  \n172\n  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n3\nRD \nMARCH\n, 2020.\n \n \n(a) & (b):     During year 2019\n-\n20, as per the Second Advance Estimates total production of \nred gram (tur)\n \nin the country including Telangana is estimated at 36.90 lakh tonnes.The \nproduction of red gram in the \nState of Telangana\n \nis estimated at 2.07 lakh tonnes.\n \n \n(c) to (e):\n \nThe Government is implementing Price Support Scheme (PSS) for \nprocurement of pulses and oilseeds\n \nincluding red gram at Minimum Support Price (MSP) \nunder the umbrella Scheme “Pradhan Mantri A\nnnadata\n \nAay\n \nSanraksH\nan\n \nAbhiyan (PM\n-\nAASHA)”.Under the PSS, as per the prescribed guidelines, Government agencies procure \npulses and oilseeds of Fair Average Quality (FAQ) at MSP from farmers in consultation with \nthe concerned State Government as and when ma\nrket price of these produce fall below the \nMSP. Further, Government has increased the MSP of red gram (tur) to Rs. 5800 per quintal \nfor 2019\n-\n20 season from Rs. 5675 per quintal of 2018\n-\n19 season.\n \n \n \n \nDuring Kharif 2019\n-\n20 season, proposals / requests have b\neen received from various \nred gram (tur) producing states including Telangana for procurement of the same under PSS. \nAccordingly, this Department has given approval to Central Nodal agencies viz., National \nAgricultural Cooperative Marketing Federation of I\nndia Ltd.(NAFED) and Food Corporation of \nIndia (FCI) to procure Red Gram under PSS in those states.\n \n \n \nDuring Kharif 2019\n-\n20, on the basis of proposal received from the Government of \nTelangana for the implementation of Price Support Scheme (PSS) for red gra\nm,\n \napproval of \nCentral Government for procurement of 47500 MTs\n \nhas been issued and against it\n \nas\n \non \n22\nnd\n \nFebruary, 2020, 45500 MTs of red gram has been procured. Based on the Second \nAdvance Estimate of 2019\n-\n20 of production of red gram in Telangana, the ap\nproved quantity \nhas been increased from 47500 MTs to 51625 MTs.\n \n******\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |173", "t": "Maternity Benefit Act", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 173  \nTO BE ANSWERED O