ions \nunder NWQSM is at Annexure-I. \n(d) Out 13,725 fluoride affected habitations identified under NW QSM, 1,507 habitations have \nbeen covered through Community Water Purification Plants.  \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure: referred in the reply to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 730 due for reply on \n06.02.2020 \n \nState wise physical progress of fluoride affected habitations under NWQSM \nS. \nNo. \nState Name Nos. of \nidentified \nHabs \nNo. of \nhabs \nCovered \nNo. of \nhabs \ncovered \nthrough \nState \nschemes/ \nquality \nimproved \nNo. of \nhabs being \ncovered \nNo. of \nhabs \nunder \nplanning \nstage \n1. Andhra Pradesh 421  249  71  25  76  \n2. Assam 155  119  3 33  - \n3. Bihar 1,043  304  435  300  4 \n4. Chhattisgarh 75  18  36  20  1 \n5. Haryana 200  33  84  78  5 \n6. Jharkhand 998  214  710  74  - \n7. Karnataka 1,038  863  59  39  77  \n8. Kerala 73  38  6 13  16  \n9. Madhya Pradesh 136  128  8 - - \n10. Maharashtra 100  47  19  27  7 \n11. Odisha 65  25  3 2 35  \n12. Punjab 285  71  20  166  28  \n13. Rajasthan 6,849  3,550  950  1,826  523  \n14. Telangana 1,041  1,040  1 - - \n15. Uttar Pradesh 200  96  19  73  12  \n16. West Bengal 1,046  161  55  627  203  \nTotal  13,725  6,956  2,479  3,303  987  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |731", "t": "Accidents Involving Two-Wheelers", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 731  \nANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nACCIDENTS  INVOLVING  TWO -WHEELERS \n \n731. SHRI BENNY BEHANAN:  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n(a)  whether there has been an increase in the number of accidents and deaths of young \ntwo-wheeler riders in various States incl uding Kerala during the last three years and \nthe current year; and  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the total number of deaths of two-wheeler riders in \nroad accidents during the sai