 to foreign companies; \n(b)  if so, the names of those companies along with the names of \nthe countries to which they belong.  \n(c)  the details of the locations for which the said com panies have \nbeen awarded contract for laying of Metro Rail Line s, State and \nplace-wise. \n(d)  whether there is a lack of companies having experti se in laying \nMetro Rail Lines in the country; and \n(e)  if not, the reasons for awarding the said contract to foreign \ncompanies? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (c):   Metro rail companies set up as 50:50 joint venture of the \nGovernment of India and respective State Government can award  \nContd...2/- \n\n-2/- \ncontracts for laying of metro rail lines either to indian companies, \nforeign companies or joint ventures of indian and f oreign \ncompanies. Only one work of laying a part of metro rail lines \nbetween Noida-Greater Noida in Uttar Pradesh has been awarded by \nthe Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (DMRC) to foreign company as a \nsole bidder i.e M/s ETF from France.  \n (d)& (e): There are a number of Indian companies c apable of laying \nmetro rail lines. Tender for laying metro rail line s are awarded \nthrough competitive bidding where there is no bar f or foreign \ncompanies to bid and get the contract subject to ot her tender \nconditions.   \n \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |735", "t": "Credit Guarantee Scheme for MSMEs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 735\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON\n \n06.02.2020\n \n \nCREDIT GUARNATEE SCHEME FOR MSMEs\n \n \n735. \n \n \nSHRI BALASHOWRY  VALLABHANENI:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nwhether Credit Guarantee Scheme (CGS) has been introduced  by the Government \nand if so, the details 