SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government has taken steps to improve the \ngenuinity and the accountability of various  sports federations in \nIndia; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) whether there is any data which shows  frauds/ \nmisappropriations/ cheatings/deceptions committed by associations \nand federations and if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) the total funds allocate d by the Government to recognized \nsports federations since 2016-17, federation and year-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI KIREN RIJIJU] \n \n(a) & (b) The National Sports Development Code of India (NSDCI) \n2011 provides for transparency and accountability in the functioning \nof National Sports Federations (NSFs). NSDCI requires NSFs to \nfollow healthy management practices, accountability, transparency, \nimpartial and transparent selection procedures, age and tenure \nrestrictions of office bearers, basic univer sal principles of good \ngovernance in sports, proper accounting procedures, prevention of \nage fraud & sexual harassment of women, and holding of elections \n\nas per model guidelines. NSFs are required to submit Utilization \nCertificates for the grants received from the Government. Accounts \nof the NSFs receiving grant of more than Rs. 1.00 crore in a year are \nsubject to audit by the Comptroller & Auditor General of India. \n \n(c) No such data is maintained by the Ministry which shows \nfrauds/misappropriations/cheatings/deceptions committed by \nassociations and federations. \n \n(d)    Budget allocation is made for different sports disciplines in \nconsultation with the concerned National Sports Federation.  The \ninformation is at Annexure. \n \n***** \n \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 741 FOR REPLY ON 06.02.2020 ASKED \nBY SHRI HIBI EDEN REGARDING ACCOUNTABILITY OF SPORT