,567 \nUttar Pradesh Allahabad 2,239 \nUttar Pradesh Jhansi 1,728 \nUttarakhand Dehradun 1,348 \nTotal 57,393 \nAverage SCP Size 1,913 \n \n \n \n\n \n \nRound 4 Cities \nState/ UT City SCP Size (Rs. Crore) \nArunachal Pradesh Itanagar 1,343 \nBihar Bihar Sharif 1,517 \nDadra and Nagar Haveli Silvassa 1,083 \nDaman and Diu Diu 1,44"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |777", "t": "Swachhata Hi Seva", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI  \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 777  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020 \n \nSwachhata Hi Seva \n \n777. SHRI SUNIL DATTATRAY TATKARE: \nSHRI SHIVAKUMAR C. UDASI: \nDR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR S.: \nDR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE: \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has organized Swachhata Hi Se va (SHS) 2019, a Jan \nAndolan for Swachhata focussing on Plastic Waste Managem ent and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(b) whether all the States have been encouraged to ban  the use of Single Use \nPlastic products during the campaign period and if so, the details thereof along \nwith the success achieved; \n \n(c) the State which has been selected and awarded as th e best in the plastic waste \nmanagement category during SHS, 2019 along with the amount al located and \nspent under SHS; and \n \n(d) whether the Government has achieved the objective of organising SHS which \nhas focussed on Plastic Waste Management and if so, the de tails thereof? \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \n(SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA) \n \n \n(a)  Swachhata Hi Seva (SHS) 2019 Campaign was organised from  11 th  \nSeptember to 2 nd  October, 2019 focusing on plastic waste management. \nAwareness campaigns were organised across the country duri ng the period. A \nnationwide shramdaan to collect and segregate plastic wa ste was organised on \nOctober 2, 2019. \n(b)  All States were advised to discourage the use of single  use plastic products. \nDuring the campaign, 6 States and 171 Districts had banned single use plastic. \n(c)  No State was selected for the award in plastic wa ste management category \nduring SHS, 2019. No separate funds were allocated for Swachhata Hi Seva \ncampaign. \n(d)  Department of Drinking Water and Sanitation, Ministry of Jal Shakti \norganised SHS 2019 with the theme “Plastic Waste Managemen t” for focused \naction towards plastic waste management and reducing u se of Single Use Plastic \n(SUP). The SHS 2019 was run from 11 th  September to 2 nd  October. All states \nwere advised to organize campaigns with massive shramdaan on  collection of \nplastic waste in all villages and towns across the countr y and following this, from \n3rd  October to 27 th  October, 2019 the collected plastic waste was  recycled and/or \neffectively disposed.  \nSwachhata Hi Seva 2019 focused on addressing management of plas tic \nwaste. It saw very encouraging response from across the  country with \nparticipation of thousands of citizens. It created aw areness among general public, \nstudents, communities, Industries, local government bodies,  Public and private \ncompanies. During the campaign, citizens participated i n large numbers in \nawareness campaigns and shramdaan activities.  \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |778", "t": "Cases Registered in MSME Samadhan Portal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 778\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020\n \n \nCASES REGISTERED IN MSME SAMADHAN PORTAL\n \n \n778.\n \n \nSHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate: \n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nthe number of cases registered in the MSME Samadhan Portal, State/year \n-\nwise;\n \n(\nb\n)\n \nwhether the Government has taken any steps to resolve the problem of delayed \npayments to MSMEs;\n \n(\nc\n)\n \nif\n \nso, the details thereof; and \n \n(\nd\n)\n \nthe features of the Credit Linked Capital Subsidy scheme?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) to\n \n(c):     Various Steps taken by the Government to resolve the problem of delayed \npayments to MSMEs include :\n-\n \n \ni\n.\n \nCreation of the MSME Samadhaan Portal.\n \nii\n.\n \nMaking it mandatory for all CPSEs to upload the information regarding their dues \non the portal.\n \niii\n.\n \nIssuance \nof notification requiring all companies to submit half\n-\nyearly returns about \ntheir dues.\n \niv\n.\n \nRoping in NeSL Information Utility to do default broadcast of buyers from MSEs \nto their other creditors.  \n \nv\n.\n \nCreation of TReDS and issuance of direction by notification t\no companies with \nturnover above Rs.500 crore and to all CPSEs to get themselves on boarded on this \nplatform.\n \n \nThe number of cases registered in the MSME Samadhan Portal, State wise and \nyear \n-\nwise are at Annexure\n-\n \nI & Annexure\n-\nII respectively.\n \n \n(\nd\n):\n \nThe Credit Linked Capital Subsidy Scheme aims at infusing modern technology in \nthe MSEs through institutional finance. Under this scheme, subsidy of 15% is provided to \nMSEs on institutional credit upto Rs.1.00 crore. \n \n \n \n******\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n-\n \nI \n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI  referred to in reply to part (a) to (c) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 778 for answer on 06.02.2020\n \n \nMinistry of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises\n \nMSME SAMADHAAN \n–\n \nDelayed Payment Monitoring Portal \n–\n \nSamadhaan Report  \n \nhttps://samadhaan.msme.gov.in\n  \nDate of Report: \n-\n \n04/02/2020 \n \n  \n \nState wise report \n(From 30/10/2017  i.e. after Launch of MSME\n-\nSamadhaan to 4.02.2020) \n \n \nS.\n \nNo.\n \nState\n \nApplications \nfiled by \nMSEs\n \nVisible to \nCouncil \nafter 15 \ndays\n \nConverted \ninto Case \nby \nMSEFC \nCou