on with \ncompletion period of 2-3 years.   \n    \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |793", "t": "Power Generation through Windmill", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 793 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020 \n \nPOWER GENERATION THROUGH WINDMILL \n793. SHRI  A. NARAYANA SWAMY \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) whether any plant of windmill power generation is functional at Chitradurga region of \nKarnataka; \n (b) if so, the details thereof along with the megawatts of electricity it will generate per year;  \n(c) whether the electricity produced is supplied to the local area and if so, the details thereof;  \n(d) whether the CSR funding is received to build the plant and if so, the details thereof;  \n(e)  whether the Government proposes to start a new wind energy project in Karnataka; and \n(f)   if so, the details thereof? \n \n                                                                     ANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (I/C) FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY, POWER and \nMoS for  SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a)&(b) Yes Sir, the installed ca pacity of wind power projects in  Chitradurga d istrict of \nKarnataka is 613.80 megawatt. The details of these projects alongwith capacity in megawatts \nare given in Annexure.  \n(c) The electricity produced from these wind power projects is supplied to the state grid. \n(d) No Sir, the CSR funding has not been used to build these wind power projects. \n(e) & (f) The wind power projects are set up by private developers based on techno-economic \nviability of the project. The Governme nt has issued ‘Guidelines for Development of Onshore \nWind Power Projects’ dated 22 October 2016 for orderly growth of wind power sector in the \ncountry, including Karnataka. \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred to in reply to parts (a) & (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No