tok   \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |878", "t": "Namami Gange Programme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 878\nANSWERED ON 06.02.2020\nNAMAMI GANGE PROGRAMME\n878. SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of the progress made by the Government in the implementation of the Namami Gange\nprogramme for conservation and rejuvenation of river Ganga;\n(b) whether it is a fact that the Governmen t has actively involved the people living on the bank of rivers,\nurban local bodies and panchayati raj institutions in the implementation of the programme;\n(c) if so, the details thereof; and\n(d) if not, the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI & SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA)\n(a) Cleaning of river is a continuous process and the Government of India is supplementing the efforts of\nthe State Governments in addressing the challenges of pollution of river Ganga by providing financial and\ntechnical assistance.\nTill December, 2019, under Namami Gange Programme, a total of 310 projects have been\nsanctioned at an estimated cost of Rs. 28,909.59 crore, out of which 114 projects have been completed and\nmade operational. Rest of the projects are at various stages of implementation.\nNamami Gange Programme includes diverse set of interventions like sewage treatment,\nindustrial effluent treatment, solid waste management etc., river front management, aviral dhara, rural\nsanitation, afforestation, biodiversity conservation.\n(b) & (c) Yes Sir. Public participation has been taken up involving concerned stakeholders including urban\nlocal bodies, panchayati raj institutions, public etc, for cleaning and rejuvenation of river Ganga.\nCommunity participation and outreach are a v ital component under Namami Gange Programme.\nNational Mission for Clean Ganga (NMCG) is involving all the stakeholders, partner organizations,\nDepartments and Ministries.\nFor maximum involvement of the local communities, IEC activities like Swachhta Pakhwada,\nSwachhta Hi Sewa, Vriksharopan Abhiyan, Ganga Yatra, Ganga Run, Ganga Utsav etc. are carried out\nregularly.\nOutdoor Publicity and Interpersonal Communication are also carried out during mass\ncongregations like Kumbh/Ardh Kumbh in Prayagraj and Haridwar, Sonpur Mela, Chatth Puja, Char Dham\nYatra, Kanvad Yatra etc.\nIn addition, NMCG organises several workshops/ seminars/ Ganga Manthan to enter into a\ndialogue with the stakeholders. Exhibitions are organized in various places and during important\nevents/fair. Short films, TVCs, TV programmes are also produced to disseminate the activities carried out\nunder the project and message on Aviral and Nirmal Ganga.\n(d) Does not arise.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |88", "t": "Excavation by ASI in Gottiprolu,Andhra Pradesh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No.*88 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.02.2020 \n \nATTACKS ON JOURNALISTS  \n*88.  SHRI ANUMULA REVANTH REDDY \n  \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION & BROADCASTING be pleased to state:- \n \n(a)   whether several cases of attacks on journalists have come to the notice of the \nGovernment; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof indicating the number of such cases reported during the \npast six years and the current year so far, State/UT-wise; \n \n(c)  whether the Press Council of India has constituted any committee to study \nincreasing incidents of attacks on journalists and if so, the details thereof and \nthe findings/ recommendations of the committee along with the action taken by \nthe Government thereon; \n \n(d)   whether Press Council of India has proposed a separate legislation to fast track \nsuch cases and payment of compensation to the family member of the victims, \nif so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; and \n \n (e)   the steps taken/being taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE: \nMINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING; AND MINISTER \nOF HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES   \n [SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR] \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (e) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 88 TO BE ANSWERED ON \n07.02.2020 ON “ATTACKS ON JOURNALISTS” \n \n(a) & (b) : „Police‟ and „Public Order‟ are State subjects under the \nSeventh Schedule of the Constitution of India and State \nGovernments are responsible for prevention, detection, registration \nand investigation of crime and for prosecuting the criminals through \ntheir law enforcement agencies.  \nCentral Government attaches highest importance to the safety \nand security of every citizen of the country including journalists. An \nadvisory specifically on safety of journalists was issued to States/ \nUTs on 20 th October 2017 requesting them to strictly enforce the \nlaw to ensure the safety and security of media persons, which is \navailable on the website www.mha.gov.in.  \n \n(c) to (e) : The Press Council of India had constituted a Sub -\nCommittee to examine the issue of  Safety of Journalists. The report \nof Sub -Committee submitted on 23.7.2015 carried various \nrecommendations with regard to safety and security of Journalists. \nThe Ministry of Home Affairs has examined the said report and \nopined that the existing laws are ad equate for protection of the \ncitizens, including journalists. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |880", "t": "New Sports Complexes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 880 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020 \n \nNew Sports Complexes \n \n880. SHRI PRADYUT BORDOLOI: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of funds allocated to the State of Assam for enhancement of \nbasic infrastructure of playgrounds, stadiums and other sports related \ninfrastructure during the last four years; \n \n(b) the details of the projects sanctioned and funds rel eased during the last \nfour years for the State of Assam, district-wise; \n \n(c) whether new sports complexes were constructed during the last five \nyears in the North Eastern States; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the expenditures involved ther ein, \nState-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI KIREN RIJIJU } \n \n(a) and (b) Sports being a State subject , the primary responsibility of \ndevelopment of sports related infrastructure  rests with the concerned \nState/Union Territory Government. The Central Government supplements \ntheir efforts by bridging the critical gaps . District-wise details of sports \ninfrastructure projects sanctioned in Assam during the last four years and \nthe current year under various schemes of the Ministry of Youth Affairs and \nSports is at Annexure-I. \n\n \n(c) and (d) The Khelo India Scheme , which deals with sports infrastructure,  \ndoes not provide for creation of mega projects such as large stadium and \nsetting up of sports complexes in the States / Union Territories. \n \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 880 TO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020 \nREGARDING “NEW SPORTS COMPLEXES ” ASKED BY SHRI PRADYUT \nBORDOLOI, HON’BLE MEMBER OF LOK SABHA \n \nANNEXURE - I \n \nDISTRICT-WISE DETAILS OF PROJECTS SANCTIONED IN ASSAM DURING THE LAST FOUR YEARS \nAND THE CURRENT YEAR \n \n(Amount in Rs. lakhs) \nS. \nNo. \nYear Name of \nscheme \nName of the project District Amount \nreleased \n1.  \n2015-\n16 \nUrban Sports \nInfrastructure \nScheme \nLaying o f Synthetic Athletic Track at North \nLakhimpur College, Lakhimpur \nLakhimpur 550.00 \n2.  Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall  at \nGovt. Boys H.S. School, Dibrugarh, under \nDibrugarh Municipality Board \nDibrugarh 600.00 \n3.  \nSAI Schemes \nEstablishment of SAG Center, Lakhimpur  Lakhimpur 1585.00 \n4.  Renovation and upgradation of infrastructure \nat SAI SAG Centre in Kokrjhar \nKokrajhar 960.00 \n5.  National \nSports \nDevelopment \nFund \nConstruction of Indoor Stadium at Abhiruchi \nInstitute of Physical Education, Guwahati \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n159.37 \n6.  2016-\n17 SAI Schemes Relaying of Wooden flooring of Multi -purpose \nhall at SAI Sub Centre Guwahati \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n123.12 \n7.  \n2017-\n18 \nKhelo India \nScheme \nLaying of Synthetic Athletic Tra ck at SAI SAG \nCentre, Kokrajhar \nKokrajhar 532.00 \n8.  Renovation / Upgradation including Laying of \nSynthetic Hockey Field in Maulana Md. \nTayabullah Hock ey Stadium, Betapara, \nGuwahati \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n450.00 \n9.  Laying of Synthetic Athletic Track including \nconstruction of sub base, drainage and chain  \nlink at SAI SAG Centre, Tinsukia. \nTinsukia 700.00 \n10.  Laying of Synthetic Hockey Tu rf at SAI SAG \nCentre, Kokrajhar \nKokrajhar 550.00 \n11.  SAI Schemes Vertical extension over existing Grand Stand \nand installation of chairs at NERC, Guwahati \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n127.00 \n12.  \n2019-\n20 \nKhelo India \nScheme \nDevelopment of infrastructure facilities for \nBihpuria Stadium Complex, Lakhimpur \nLakhimpur 150.00 \n13.  Renovation of Cyclin g Velodrome at LNIPE, \nGuwahati \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n100.00 \n14.  Renovation, and up -gradation of va rious \nsports infrastructure in Assam for Khelo India \nYouth Games 2020 \nKamrup \nMetropolitan \n1450.00 \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |881", "t": "New Motor Vehicles Act", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 881 \nANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nNEW MOTOR VEHICLES ACT  \n \n881.  SHRI RAJIV RANJAN SINGH ALIAS LALAN SINGH: \n SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nlM+d ifjogu vkSj jktekxZ ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the States can reduce the penalties under the new Motor Vehicles Act; and  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the name of  States which have already reduced the \npenalties under the new Act? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) and (b) The Section 200 of the Motor vehicles Act, 1988 after the Motor Vehicles \n(Amendment) Act, 2019, recently passed by the Parliament, read s -“200 Composition of certain \noffences – (1) Any offence whether  committed before or after the commencement of this Act \npunishable under section 177, section 178, section 179, section 180, section 181, section 182, sub-\nsection (1) or sub-section (3) or sub -section (4) of section 182A, section 182B, sub -section (1) or \nsub-section (2) of section 183, section 184 only to the e xtent of use of handheld  communication \ndevices, section 186, section 189, sub -section (2) of section 190,  section 192, section 192A, \nsection 194, section 194A, section 194B, section 194C, section 194D, section 194E, section 194F, \nsection 196, section 198 , may either before or after the institution of the prosecution, be  \ncompounded by such officers or authorities and for such amount as the State Government may, by \nnotification in the Official Gazette, specify in this behalf.” \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |882", "t": "Distance-based Criteria for Toll Plazas on NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS\n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n882\n \n \nANSWERED ON \n6\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, \n2020\n \nDISTANCE\n-\nBASED CRITERIA FOR TOLL PLAZAS ON NHS\n \n882\n.\n \nKUNWAR DANISH ALI\n:\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS\n \nlM+d\n \nifjogu\n \nvkSj\n \njktekxZ\n \nea=h\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n(a) whether it is a fact that passengers have to face\n \nthe  loss  of  money  and  time  due  to  existence  \nof  toll\n \nplazas at short intervals on National Highways (NHs) in\n \nthe  country;\n \n(b)  if  so,  the  \ndetails  thereof;\n \n(c)  the distance based criteria for setting up of toll\n \nplazas on NHs according to National Highways \nAuthority\n \nof India (NHAI); and\n \n(d)  the  number  of  toll  plazas  in  the  country\n \nparticularly  in  Uttar  Pradesh  which  do  not  \nfol\nlow  the\n \ndistance\n-\nbased  criteria  for  setting  up  of  toll  plazas\n?\n \nANSWER\n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS\n \n(\nSHRI \nNITIN JAIRAM GADKARI\n)\n \n(a)\n \n&(b) \nUser fee \nis\n \ncollected for use of the section of National Highway at specified rate\ns\n \nmentioned in \nrespective\n \nfee notification\n \npublished\n \nas per applicable National Highways Fee Rules\n. \nTo offer\n \nseamless movement and sav\ne\n \ntime \nat\n \nuser fee plaza\ns\n \non National Highway\ns\n, Government \nhas mandate to convert all lanes of user fee plaza as \nexclusive \nFASTag \nlanes\n \ne\nxcept one \nhybrid \nlane \non each direction. As such, there is no loss of money and time.\n \n(c) \nAs per Rule 8(2) of the National Highways Fee (Determination of Rates and Collection)\n \nRules, \n2008\n \n–\n \n“An\ny other fee plaza on same section of national highway and in \nthe same direction shall not \nbe established within\n \na distance of sixty kilometers:\n \n \nProvided that where the executing authority deems necessary, it may for reasons to be \nrecorded in writing, establish or allow the concessionaire to establish another \nfee\n \npl\naza within\n \na \ndistance of sixty kilometers:\n \n \nProvided further that a \nfee\n \nplaza may be established within a distance of sixty kilometres \nfrom another \nfee\n \nplaza if such \nfee\n \nplaza is for collection of fee for a permanent bridge, bypass or \ntunnel.\n” This rule is\n \napplicable for \nBuild\n,\n \nOperate \n& \nTransfer (\nBOT\n)\n \nprojects taken up on or after \n05.12.2008\n \nand all public funded projects\n.\n \n(d) \nAll user fee plaza\ns\n \nare established in accordance with \napplicable \nN\national Highways \nFee rules.\n \n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |883", "t": "Loan Facility for Setting up of New Industries in MSME Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 883\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 06.02.2020\n \n \nLOAN FACILITY FOR SETTING UP OF NEW INDUSTRY IN MSME \nSECTOR\n \n \n883\n \n \nDR. RAM SHANKAR KATHERIA:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nwhether the Government has formulated any scheme to provide easy loan \nfacility for setting up new industry in MSME sector to ensure welfare of the poor;\n \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nif so, the details ther\neof; and\n \n \n(\nc\n)\n \nthe number of people got benefited so far under above scheme?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN \nGADKARI)\n \n \n(a) to (c):\n \n \nT\nhe Ministry of Micro, Sma\nll and Medium Enterprises (MSME\n) \nimplements credit linked subsidy scheme namely Prime Minister’s Employment \nGeneration Programme (PMEGP) to promote self\n-\nemployment  opportunities through \nestablishment of micro\n-\nenterprises in non\n-\nagriculture sector.  5,87,416 employment \nopportunities wer\ne created by giving margin money subsidy of Rs\n.\n \n2070 crore  to \n73,427 projects during the year 2018\n-\n19. \n \n \nGovernment of India also implements Pradhan Mantri MUDRA Yojana \n(PMMY) to provide collateral free loans upto Rs 10 lakh.  \n \n \n****\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|3|UNSTARRED |884", "t": "Projects Undertaken in Santhal Pargana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 884 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 06, 2020 \n \nPROJECTS UNDERTAKEN IN SANTHAL PARGANA \n NO. 884.     DR. NISHIKANT DUBEY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBANAFFAIRSbe ple ased \nto state: \n(a) whether the Union Government has undertaken any  projects \nfor enhancing basic amenities in Santhal Pargana of  \nJharkhand and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) the funds earmarked for this purpose since last  three years;    \nand \n(c) the time line by which the projects would be completed? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n (SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n(a)to(c) The Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs( MoHUA) \nfacilitates and assists States/Union Territories (U Ts) \nincluding the towns in Santhanal Parganas of  Jhark hand, \nthrough its flagship Missions - Swachh Bharat Missi on-\nUrban(SBM-U), Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urb an \nTransformation (AMRUT), Smart Cities Mission (SCM),  \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban)(PMAY-U), to impr ove \nurban infrastructure, enhance basic amenities and q uality of \nlife in cities and towns covered under these Missions. Central \nAssistance is allocated and released to the States/ UTs as a \nwhole, and not for any particular area therein. The  States in \nturn release funds to cities/towns. Infrastructure projects \ntake about 3 years or morefor completion after awar d of \ncontracts. Details of development projects taken up  in \ntowns/cities in Santhal Pargana area are given in t he \nAnnexure. \n****** \n\nAnnexure referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Unstarre d Question No 884 regarding \n‘Projects undertaken in Santhal Pargana’ for answer on 06 February, 2020. \nProjects undertaken in cities/towns of Santhal Parganas area \nAtal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation(AMRUT)  \nProjects in Deogarh city  \n