y in Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh and Rajasthan; and\n(c) the funds allocated/proposed to be allocated for the same and their actual utilization,\nState/UT-wise?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a) to (c): Under NHM support is provided to States/UTs for strengthening of their\nhealthcare system including modernisation/upgradation of Govt. hospitals in rural areas of the\ncountry. This support is based on proposal received from States in the form of Programme\nImplementation Plan (PIPs). The proposals are appraised in National Programme Coordination\nCommittee (NPCC) meetings and approvals are accorded to States/UTs in the form of record of\nproceedings (RoPs).\nPublic Health and hospitals being a State subject, i t is up to the States to plan and\nimplement state specific action plans including upgrading/modernizing health centres based on\ngap assessment and felt need.\nThe State/UT wise details of approvals for upgradation of Hospitals, New Construction\nincluding utilization of funds under NHM during the last three years from the FY 2016-17 to\n2018-19 is at Annexure.\n………………..\n\nAnnexure\nStatement Showing the State/UTs wise Approval & Utilization of Funds under Hospital\nStrengthening and New Constructions/ Renovation and Setting up from the\nF.Y. 2016-17 to 2018-19\nRs. In Lakhs\nS.No. State 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19\nApproval Exp. Approval Exp. Approval Exp.\nA.\nHigh\nFocus\nStates\n1 Bihar 12657.33 4633.51 19904.63 664.10 48606.76 5112.58\n2 Chattisgarh 3992.80 12292.34 12510.51 10477.47 17363.34 8917.39\n3\nHimachal\nPradesh 3879.11 3931.17 5363.32 3279.32 4850.91 5814.97\n4\nJammu &\nKashmir 2924.43 3844.86 1991.64 1424.44 3539.14 3912.88\n5 Jharkhand 5221.32 209.10 1867.07 454.26 6689.56 2754.14\n6\nMadhya\nPradesh 21004.94 18146.00 23270.12 15025.54 29635.64 13325.15\n7 Orissa 30582.98 22391.56 26957.09 12606.82 26429.56 22103.91\n8 Rajasthan 33253.21 25520.11 28619.01 26092.66 252